// How the debug view of shroud and fog is drawn (WP8.1, docs/rules/vision.md). Read by
// sf_data::vision_look, compiled into the game, checked when it is parsed. Debug only: the real
// look (soft edges, ghosts of seen structures, a filtered minimap) is WP8.3 and WP8.4. It draws
// from the local player's own bitsets over the whole picture, units of the other side included, so
// it is not a fair view: do not play with it on. Switch it on with the "Fog of war (debug)"
// checkbox of the F1 panel or `--debug-fog`. Colours sRGB, alpha last. No checksum depends on this
// file.
(
    // Cells never seen.
    shroud: (0, 0, 0, 215),
    // Cells seen before but not now.
    fog: (10, 14, 24, 120),
    // A cell of the building placement preview that holds something the player cannot see (the
    // sim says structure or unit; the cell is not in sight now): drawn in this neutral colour, not
    // as the red of a blocked cell, so the preview does not show what is hidden (docs/rules/fog_look.md).
    placement_unknown: (150, 150, 160, 110),
    // The most cells of one row drawn as one quad (so that a quad follows a slope).
    run_cells: 8,
)
